{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:828a055542617d95", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Alternative mutual funds (sometimes called alt funds or liquid alts) are publicly offered, SEC-registered mutual funds that hold non-traditional investments or use complex investment and trading strategies.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual funds, sometimes called alt funds, are publicly offered mutual funds that may invest in non-traditional assets—such as commodities or global real estate—or use complex strategies such as short selling or derivatives. These approaches may offer different sources of diversification or returns, but can also bring additional risks and higher costs. Their objectives and strategies vary, so understanding a particular fund’s risks and expenses is important.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 235}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:828a055542617d95", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Alternative mutual funds (sometimes called alt funds or liquid alts) are publicly offered, SEC-registered mutual funds that hold non-traditional investments or use complex investment and trading strategies.", "question": "What is one key way alternative mutual funds differ from more traditional mutual funds?", "answer": "They often hold non-traditional investments or use complex investment and trading strategies.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 371}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:828a055542617d95", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "However, alt funds differ from hedge funds in several important ways.", "question": "Misconception: Alternative mutual funds are simply hedge funds with a different name.", "answer": "Correction: Alternative mutual funds may use investments and strategies similar to hedge funds, but they are not the same. They are mutual funds subject to certain regulatory safeguards, and investors can purchase their shares publicly. They can still involve complex strategies and additional risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 228}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d60e10b08ec86e5d", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Investment Strategies", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Alt funds generally use more complex investment and trading strategies than more traditional mutual funds.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual funds may use strategies such as short selling stocks or using derivatives. Some follow “absolute return” or “market neutral” approaches that seek positive returns even when stock markets fall. These strategies describe a goal, not a guaranteed result, and may bring higher costs and additional risks than strategies used by traditional mutual funds.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 232}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d60e10b08ec86e5d", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Investment Strategies", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Alt funds generally use more complex investment and trading strategies than more traditional mutual funds. For example, alt funds may sell stocks short, use derivatives, or follow \"absolute return\" or “market neutral” strategies that seek positive returns even when the stock markets fall.", "question": "What are some strategies alternative mutual funds may use, and what is one risk associated with them?", "answer": "Alternative mutual funds may sell stocks short, use derivatives, or use market-neutral strategies that seek positive returns even when stock markets fall. These complex strategies can involve additional risks and may result in higher costs than traditional mutual funds.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 203}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d60e10b08ec86e5d", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Investment Strategies", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "strategies that seek positive returns even when the stock markets fall.  However, these strategies may result in higher costs and additional risks than traditionally managed funds.", "question": "Misconception: Alternative mutual funds that use market-neutral strategies are guaranteed to make money when stock markets fall. Is that true?", "answer": "No. Some alternative mutual funds use strategies that seek positive returns even when stock markets fall, but that is an objective, not a guarantee. These strategies can also involve additional risks and higher costs.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1758, "output_tokens": 224}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:0d5515b7e3cdcafb", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds vs. Hedge Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "As mutual funds, alt funds are regulated under the Investment Company Act of 1940, which provides certain safeguards. Hedge funds are not required to follow these regulations, and therefore may pursue non-traditional strategies and investments without the same regulatory safeguards.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual funds and hedge funds can use similar investments and strategies, but they do not have the same regulatory safeguards. Alternative mutual funds are regulated under the Investment Company Act of 1940, which includes limits on illiquid investments and borrowings and requires investors to be able to sell their shares at any time. Hedge funds are not required to follow these regulations. Access also differs: any investor may purchase alternative mutual funds, while hedge fund shares are limited to accredited investors or qualified purchasers. These differences do not mean that alternative mutual funds have no risks; their complex strategies can bring additional risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": false, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 509}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:0d5515b7e3cdcafb", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds vs. Hedge Funds", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Hedge funds are not required to follow these regulations, and therefore may pursue non-traditional strategies and investments without the same regulatory safeguards.", "question": "How do alternative mutual funds differ from hedge funds in regulatory safeguards?", "answer": "Alternative mutual funds are regulated under the Investment Company Act of 1940, which provides safeguards such as limits on illiquid investments and restrictions on borrowings and debt. Hedge funds are not required to follow these regulations, so they do not have the same safeguards.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 189}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:0d5515b7e3cdcafb", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Mutual Funds vs. Hedge Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "As mutual funds, alt funds are regulated under the Investment Company Act of 1940, which provides certain safeguards.", "question": "Misconception: Alternative mutual funds are simply hedge funds sold to the public, so they do not have mutual-fund regulatory safeguards.", "answer": "Correction: Alternative mutual funds may use investments and strategies similar to hedge funds, but they are mutual funds regulated under the Investment Company Act of 1940. The source says this regulation provides safeguards, including limits on illiquid investments and borrowings, and requires the fund to let investors sell their shares at any time. Hedge funds are not required to follow these regulations.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 297}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:be8c3d81b802d69c", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Diversification with Alternative Assets", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These investments can sometimes offer greater diversification or different returns than more traditional investments such as stocks, bonds, and cash.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual funds may invest in assets such as global real estate, start-up companies, or commodities like gold or oil. Including different asset types can sometimes provide greater diversification or different returns than relying on traditional investments such as stocks, bonds, and cash. This is not a guarantee of lower risk: alternative funds have unique characteristics and may involve additional risks from their investments or strategies.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 344}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:be8c3d81b802d69c", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Diversification with Alternative Assets", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "These investments can sometimes offer greater diversification or different returns than more traditional investments such as stocks, bonds, and cash.", "question": "How can alternative mutual funds provide diversification through alternative assets?", "answer": "Some alternative mutual funds invest in assets such as real estate or commodities, which may provide exposure beyond traditional stocks, bonds, and cash. This can sometimes offer greater diversification or different returns, though it does not guarantee lower risk or better performance.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 210}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:be8c3d81b802d69c", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Diversification with Alternative Assets", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "These investments can sometimes offer greater diversification or different returns than more traditional investments such as stocks, bonds, and cash. In addition to the usual market and investment risks associated with traditional mutual funds, alt funds may face additional risks to the extent they use relatively complex investment and trading strategies.", "question": "Misconception: Because an alternative mutual fund invests in different types of assets, it eliminates investment risk.", "answer": "Diversification may sometimes provide exposure to different returns or broaden the types of investments held, but it does not eliminate risk. Alternative mutual funds still face market and investment risks, and complex strategies may add further risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": false, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 562}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:08d057604e7c18cf", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Complex Strategies and Investment Risk", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "these potential risks can include use of derivatives and leverage, futures contracts, short selling and swaps.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual funds may use complex strategies such as short selling, derivatives, or strategies intended to seek positive returns even when stock markets fall. These approaches can bring additional risks and higher costs compared with traditionally managed funds. The particular risks depend on the strategy used and may involve leverage, futures contracts, short selling, or swaps. A fund’s strategy is therefore important to understand when considering its risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 173}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:08d057604e7c18cf", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Complex Strategies and Investment Risk", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "However, these strategies may result in higher costs and additional risks than traditionally managed funds.", "question": "Why can complex strategies in alternative mutual funds create additional risks and costs?", "answer": "Strategies such as short selling or using derivatives can be more complex than traditional fund strategies, and the source notes they may lead to higher costs and additional risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 160}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:08d057604e7c18cf", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Complex Strategies and Investment Risk", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "In addition to the usual market and investment risks associated with traditional mutual funds, alt funds may face additional risks to the extent they use relatively complex investment and trading strategies.", "question": "Misconception: If an alternative mutual fund aims to reduce swings or diversify investments, its complex strategies cannot add risk. Is that true?", "answer": "No. A goal of reducing swings or diversifying does not mean the fund is free of added risk. Alternative mutual funds may face risks beyond those of traditional mutual funds when they use complex strategies, including strategies involving derivatives, leverage, futures, short selling, or swaps.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 249}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:2a5a955fc6d2d7aa", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Fund Fees and Expenses", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Alternative mutual funds may have higher expenses than their traditional mutual fund peers. The strategies pursued by alt funds are often complex and may require significant expertise and active management, which increases costs. In addition, the more complex strategies themselves may generate additional expenses.", "question": null, "answer": "Alternative mutual fund expenses depend partly on how the fund is managed. Compared with traditional mutual funds, an alt fund may have higher expenses because complex strategies can require specialized expertise and active management, and the strategies themselves may add costs. This does not mean alt funds always cost more: the source also says investors generally pay lower fees for alternative mutual funds than for hedge funds. When comparing funds, distinguish which type of fund is being used as the comparison.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 491}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:2a5a955fc6d2d7aa", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Fund Fees and Expenses", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "The strategies pursued by alt funds are often complex and may require significant expertise and active management, which increases costs.", "question": "Why may alternative mutual funds have higher operating expenses than traditional mutual funds?", "answer": "Their complex strategies can require specialized expertise and active management, and the strategies themselves may generate additional expenses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 156}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:2a5a955fc6d2d7aa", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Alternative Fund Fees and Expenses", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Alternative mutual funds may have higher expenses than their traditional mutual fund peers.", "question": "Misconception: Alternative mutual funds always have lower expenses than traditional mutual funds because they are mutual funds.", "answer": "Not necessarily. Alternative mutual funds may have higher expenses than traditional mutual funds. Their complex strategies can require significant expertise and active management, and may generate additional expenses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1760, "output_tokens": 209}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ea2fc53ac0d1ca9b", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Evaluating Fund Managers and Performance History", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Many alternative mutual funds have limited performance histories. For example, many were launched after 2008, so it is not known how they would perform in a down market. They may perform differently than broad indexes such as the S&P 500. Fund Manager: Learn as much as you can about the fund manager, such as how long he or she has managed the fund and his or her prior management or professional experience.", "question": null, "answer": "When evaluating an alternative mutual fund, consider both the manager and the limits of the fund’s performance record. Find out how long the manager has managed the fund and review their prior management or professional experience; the prospectus may provide some of this information. Also note that many alternative mutual funds have limited histories, so their results may not show how they would perform in a down market, and they may behave differently from broad indexes. Read the prospectus and shareholder reports to learn more about the fund.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 369}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ea2fc53ac0d1ca9b", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Evaluating Fund Managers and Performance History", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Learn as much as you can about the fund manager, such as how long he or she has managed the fund and his or her prior management or professional experience.", "question": "When evaluating an alternative mutual fund’s manager, what information should an investor review?", "answer": "Review how long the manager has managed the fund and their prior management or professional experience. The fund’s prospectus may provide some of this information.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 332}}
{"id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ea2fc53ac0d1ca9b", "source_id": "9ff9d7bf9c071762", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/investment-products/mutual-funds-and-exchange-traded-funds-etfs/alternative-mutual-funds", "topic": "Alternative Mutual Funds", "subtopic": "Evaluating Fund Managers and Performance History", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "For example, many were launched after 2008, so it is not known how they would perform in a down market.", "question": "Misconception: A fund manager’s prior experience tells you how an alternative mutual fund will perform in a down market, even if the fund has a limited performance history.", "answer": "A manager’s prior management or professional experience is useful to learn about, but it does not establish how the fund itself will perform in a down market. Many alternative mutual funds have limited performance histories, and how they would perform in a down market may not be known.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 1762, "output_tokens": 332}}
